# November 22, 2026: Amsterdam's standing buildings and the Mohawk shore west of it, Montgomery County, New York
# (region mohawk, drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny). The Atlas had, in the city of Amsterdam, only the
# vanished Main Street, the Sweet canal store, the dams on the Chuctanunda and the Mohasco power house, and nothing
# between Tribes Hill and Sprakers but the Fonda courthouse and Fultonville. Standing places mostly: the city hall
# (the Sanford mansion), the Carnegie library, the armory ("Amsterdam Castle"), the Greene mansion, two schools now
# apartments, the former Temple of Israel, St. Stanislaus church, the post office with its murals and the Green Hill
# Cemetery; then Danascara Place at Tribes Hill, the old Caughnawaga burying ground in Fonda, Barge Canal Lock E13 at
# the Thruway's Mohawk Valley Welcome Center, the Windfall Dutch barn at Salt Springville and Pawling Hall in Hagaman.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); HMdb marker pages, the Thruway
# Authority's welcome-centre page, the Diocese of Albany's page for St. Stanislaus, the Town of Minden's pages, the
# county tourism listing for the Windfall barn and the National Register form for Danascara Place, through
# tools/page.py.
